    <html:div><html:h2>MaP Endpoint Capability Statement — UNVERIFIED CAPABILITY CATALOG (ALL OFF)</html:h2><html:table><html:tbody><html:tr><html:th>Responsible Organization / Service</html:th><html:td>DirectTrust Payload Testing Tool</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:th>Direct Address</html:th><html:td>mapFramework@Direct3.DirectTrust.org</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:th>Supported Use Case</html:th><html:td>cc-maternal-health-birth</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:th>FHIR Version</html:th><html:td>R4 (4.0.1)</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:th>Last Updated</html:th><html:td>2026-10-14</html:td></html:tr></html:tbody></html:table><html:h3>Candidate Capabilities — Disabled Until Verified</html:h3><html:p>The entries below identify potential capabilities for future implementation and verification. Every Sender Actor, Receiver Actor, and Preferred flag defaults to No. Turn on a specific role only after it is implemented and verified with recorded evidence. TX6 remains catalogued as a native IHE query outside the Direct exchange scope; do not enable it as a Direct capability.</html:p><html:table><html:thead><html:tr><html:th>Transaction</html:th><html:th>Sender Actor</html:th><html:th>Receiver Actor</html:th></html:tr></html:thead><html:tbody><html:tr><html:td>send-outpatient-visit-notification</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-admission-notification</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-birth-notification</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-discharge-notification</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-documents</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>query-for-documents</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-patient-update</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>send-workflow-status</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr></html:tbody></html:table><html:h3>Metadata Packaging</html:h3><html:table><html:thead><html:tr><html:th>Representation</html:th><html:th>Sender Actor</html:th><html:th>Receiver Actor</html:th><html:th>Preferred</html:th></html:tr></html:thead><html:tbody><html:tr><html:td>Payload containing XDM Metadata</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr><html:tr><html:td>Payload containing FHIR Metadata</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td><html:td>No</html:td></html:tr></html:tbody></html:table><html:h3>Workflow Activity Task Processing Policy</html:h3><html:p>No Workflow Activity Task processing capability is asserted by this baseline. Support for receiving, validating, and executing Task instructions must be assessed separately under the applicable Transaction Definition. TX8 support must not be inferred merely from Task presence.</html:p><html:h3>Implementation Note</html:h3><html:p>This DRAFT catalog is not a verified deployed CapabilityStatement. Do not use it for Directory discovery, live routing, or conformance claims. Before enabling any flag, document the test evidence, approving reviewer, and verification date. Keep preferred=false until a supported representation is verified and approved as preferred.</html:p></html:div></text>
